  "id": "COMPOUND:18839 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "Plakortide N is implicated in the biological pathway leading to VMRC-MELG through multiple independent routes. The first pathway links Plakortide N to Malme-3M, which is a target of Notoamide B, and Notoamide B further targets VMRC-MELG. The second pathway provides a longer chain of targets, connecting Plakortide N to a compound that directly targets VMRC-MELG. The third pathway shows that Plakortide N also targets Malme-3M, which is a target of Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, and this compound also targets VMRC-MELG. These findings collectively suggest that Plakortide N may act through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the inhibition of VMRC-MELG. The mechanisms are not fully elucidated, but the shared target of Malme-3M and the direct targeting of VMRC-MELG indicate a potential role for Plakortide N in modulating the activity of VMRC-MELG. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Plakortide N and VMRC-MELG, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mode of action and the significance of the intermediaries.",
